coder › Done on branch `fix/overlaps-exclusive-end` (2 commits).

What changed:
- `src/range.ts` — `overlaps` now:
  - Parses all four endpoints with `Date.parse`; unparseable `start`/`end` throws `TypeError` with message `Invalid date: <value>` (so the offending value is included).
  - Throws `RangeError` when a range's `end < start` (message includes both values: `Range end is before start: <start> > <end>`).
  - Treats end as exclusive: `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, so touching ranges (`a.end === b.start`) return `false`.
  - Returns `false` if either range is zero-length (`start === end`), including a zero-length range vs itself.
- `src/range.test.ts` — kept the existing test; added 6 tests: touch-both-orders → false, same-start → true, zero-length (self/left/right) → false, bad start in either arg → TypeError containing value, bad end in either arg → TypeError containing value, backwards range in either arg → RangeError.

Decisions not in the plan:
- Error message wording (`Invalid date: …` / `Range end is before start: … > …`) — plan only required the type and that the TypeError message include the value.
- Validation order: both ranges are fully validated (parse + ordering) before the empty-range early-`false`; so a backwards range still throws even against an empty range.

